{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q416894","formula":"Cl₂Cr","hill":"Cl2Cr","elements":["Cl","Cr"],"composition":{"Cl":2.0,"Cr":1.0},"names":{"en":"Chromous chloride","ru":"Хлорид хрома(II)"},"descriptions":{"en":"Chromium(II) chloride describes inorganic compounds with the formula CrCl2(H2O)n. The anhydrous solid is white when pure, however commercial samples are often grey or green; it is hygroscopic and readily dissolves in water to give bright blue air-sensitive solutions of the tetrahydrate Cr(H2O)4Cl2. Chromium(II) chloride has no commercial uses but is used on a laboratory-scale for the synthesis of other chromium complexes.","ru":"Хлори́д хро́ма(II) CrCl2 — белые, чрезвычайно гигроскопичные кристаллы, растворимые в воде. Нерастворим в диэтиловом эфире, малорастворим в спирте."},"fame":29,"pubchemCid":24871,"mass":122.9,"charge":0,"smiles":"Cl[Cr]Cl","inchikey":"XBWRJSSJWDOUSJ-UHFFFAOYSA-L","iupac":"dichlorochromium","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-22857","atoms":24,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[6.165,0.0,0.0],[0.0,6.93,0.0],[0.0,0.0,3.489]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":3.083,"y":3.465,"z":1.744,"el":"Cr"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Cr"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":6.978,"el":"Cr"},{"x":0.0,"y":6.93,"z":0.0,"el":"Cr"},{"x":0.0,"y":6.93,"z":6.978,"el":"Cr"},{"x":6.165,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Cr"},{"x":6.165,"y":0.0,"z":6.978,"el":"Cr"},{"x":6.165,"y":6.93,"z":0.0,"el":"Cr"},{"x":6.165,"y":6.93,"z":6.978,"el":"Cr"},{"x":4.848,"y":0.948,"z":1.744,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.317,"y":5.982,"z":1.744,"el":"Cl"},{"x":4.4,"y":4.413,"z":0.0,"el":"Cl"},{"x":4.4,"y":4.413,"z":6.978,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.765,"y":2.517,"z":0.0,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.765,"y":2.517,"z":6.978,"el":"Cl"},{"x":3.083,"y":3.465,"z":5.233,"el":"Cr"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":3.489,"el":"Cr"},{"x":0.0,"y":6.93,"z":3.489